{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# J2 — Extract the Jira-family shared layer out of the Cloud adapter\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`adapters/jira/` currently owns units that are Jira-family-general, not Cloud-specific: the local↔Jira value\nmaps and sanitizers (`jira_fields.py`), the `rebar-id` identity convention (`identity.py`), the link relation\nvocabulary (`jira_fields._RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK`), and the absence-probe classifier (`probe.py`). PR #120\nconsumed these from a second adapter as **private** cross-package imports, which ADR 0035 never sanctioned —\nits seam is one level deep, core ⇄ adapter, with `adapters/jira/` as one backend's concrete implementation.\n\n## Approach\n\nCreate `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/` and move the **non-location-pinned** units\ninto it with **public** names, then re-point the Cloud adapter's imports. Behavior is unchanged and proven so by\nthe characterization oracles pinned in J1 [rebar:acb2-1823-2f0d-415b], which must pass untouched across this\nchange.\n\n**The move set is exactly the three modules that carry no by-path load references:**\n\n- `jira_fields.py` — the value maps (`_LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA`, `_LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA`), the sanitizers\n  (`_sanitize_label`, `_sanitize_summary`, `_sanitize_description`, `_sanitize_comment`), `InvalidLabelError`,\n  and the link-relation vocabulary (`_RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK`).\n- `identity.py` — `JiraIdentityConvention`.\n- `probe.py` — `classify_probe_response`, `RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES`.\n\nVerified at plan time with the ADR-prescribed grep\n(`lazy_load(|_load_sibling_keyed(|spec_from_file_location(`) plus a filename-string sweep over `src/` and\n`tests/`: these three appear in **no** by-path load site.\n\n**`outbound_fields.py`, `adf.py`, and `comment_limits.py` do NOT move** — they are location-pinned per ADR 0035\n§(a), and the pin is live, not merely historical:\n\n- `adapters/jira/adf.py` is loaded by path from `inbound_fields.py:36` and\n  `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:69` (`lazy_load(_ADF_KEY, \"adapters/jira/adf.py\")`), plus ~13 test files.\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py` is loaded by path from `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_config.py:193`,\n  `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_roundtrip.py:72`, and\n  `tests/interfaces/store/test_commits_on_ticket.py:121`.\n- `adapters/jira/comment_limits.py` is loaded by path from ~9 test files.\n\nSo the units inside them — `_map_local_to_jira_fields`, `_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_STATUS`, `_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_PRIORITY`, and\nthe ADF encoder — are shared **by dependency inversion, not relocation**: the pinned module imports the\n`jira_family` contracts (never the reverse) and is parameterized by them, so DC reuses one implementation with\nno file moving and `_loader.py` untouched. Relocating them is ADR 0035 Phase 2's work and is out of scope; if\nthis story appears to require moving a pinned file, stop and record the blocker rather than moving it.\n\nPer ADR 0035 decision 4, **no re-export shims** are left at the old paths: tests patch module-qualified, so a\nshim would create a patch-binding bug. Every importer and every `mock.patch` string is updated in this same\nchange, and each moved module keeps exactly one canonical path.\n\n`adapters/jira/`'s ACLI transport (`acli*.py`) is explicitly **not** moved and not modified: it is the\nCloud-specific, live-validated part.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** promoting these into the backend-neutral core. They are Jira-specific — a GitHub\nbackend would want none of them — so the neutral core is the wrong home and would re-create the coupling ADR\n0035's Phase 2 removed.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** leaving them in `adapters/jira/` and importing across adapters (PR #120's approach).\nIt makes a concrete backend double as a shared library with no contract, and points a dependency edge sideways\nbetween siblings.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/` (new package).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/` — `jira_fields.py`, `identity.py`, `probe.py` relocated;\n  `backend.py` and `outbound_fields.py` imports updated; `acli*.py`, `adf.py`, `comment_limits.py` untouched in\n  location.\n- Every internal importer and every test `mock.patch` string naming the old paths.\n- **Out of scope:** moving any location-pinned module, and any edit to `_loader.py`.\n\n## Testing\n\nContract tier plus the pinned characterization oracles: the mechanism is a relocation, so the oracle is that\nobservable behavior is identical and that no import or patch target dangles.\n\n- happy path: the full existing suite passes, including J1's exact-value characterization assertions, with no\n  edits to those assertions.\n- structural oracle: a test asserts no module under `adapters/jira/` imports a name from a sibling adapter\n  package, and that `adapters/jira_family/` imports from neither `adapters/jira/` nor\n  `adapters/jira_datacenter/` — pinning the acyclic direction this epic exists to establish.\n- negative control: `grep` confirms no re-export shim module remains at any old path.\n- collateral invariant: the reconciler's dynamic loader still resolves every by-path module (the existing loader\n  tests pass unchanged), and a test asserts each pinned filename (`adapters/jira/adf.py`,\n  `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py`, `adapters/jira/comment_limits.py`) still exists at its pinned path —\n  proving no location-pinned file moved.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `make test` passes with J1's characterization assertions unmodified\n- [ ] no module under `adapters/jira/` imports a name from a sibling adapter package, and no module under\n      `adapters/jira_family/` imports from `adapters/jira/` or `adapters/jira_datacenter/` — verified by grep at\n      this story's merge time (the reciprocal check on `adapters/jira_datacenter/` is J7's AC, since that\n      package does not exist yet)\n- [ ] no re-export shim exists at any pre-move path (verified by `grep` for the old module names)\n- [ ] every `mock.patch(` string in `tests/` naming a moved module resolves to the new path (`make test` green\n      is the check, since a stale patch target raises)\n- [ ] `adapters/jira/acli*.py` are byte-identical to their pre-change state (`git diff --stat` shows no change)\n- [ ] `adapters/jira/adf.py`, `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py`, and `adapters/jira/comment_limits.py` still\n      exist at those exact paths, and `_loader.py` is unchanged (`git diff --stat` shows neither a rename nor an\n      edit to `_loader.py`)"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785288552686030001,"uuid":"15d77dab-c2e4-4304-8736-bd014951fc5b"}